E!-Page is as long freely Distributable as long as the Archive Contents 
stay intact! At least these files should be in the Archive:

E!-Page1.2.rexx ........... Main Program ....................... 3002 Bytes
E!-Page1.2.doc ............ This Doc-File ...................... 2780 Bytes
fonts/pearl.font .......... required Font-File .................. 264 Bytes
fonts/pearl/8 ............. required Font-File ................. 2616 Bytes
libs/apig.library ......... apig.library by Ronnie E. Kelly ... 61220 Bytes 
libs/apig.doc ............. docs to the apig.library ......... 169198 Bytes  
libs/rexxsupport.library .. required library ................... 2524 Bytes

Full Archive Size: 80078


Installation:

First Copy E!-Page1.2.rexx into your DOORS:, if you haven't assigned it, you
should know yourself where to find it. Copy all the fonts/#? and libs/#?
Files to the matching dirs on your SYS: Partition.


Then edit the EX.BBSMenus File. Primary you have to find the following line:

610,  C,  0,  "1-32", ""

Now insert the following text between the two '"'s:

\#0Doors:E!-Page1.2.rexx

Save the File, and select the Master Window's Pull-Down-Menu
Extras/Re-Load/Menus. Thats all for the Installation..



Now make a Sysop-Login to your BBS, and type C at the main Menu. If everything is installed
correctly you should see something like that:

+-------------< Enter a reason for Chat (max. 70 Chars) >----------------+
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  ---------  E!-Page1.2 - Coded by the ACP-Development in 2/95  --------
   Amiga Crackpoint --- * --- +43 2252 46519 --- * --- 2 Lines USR V.34

Enter a chat-reason and... a window pops up at the Workbench Screen! If you
feel to chat to the paging User press any key in the Window and the E! Screen
will open, otherwise dont touch it - it closes itself after a few seconds.


Have fun with E!-Page! If you find some bugs or have ideas how to enhance
E!-Page in future, simply send a NetMail or Crashmail to

